# Pi workflow reference

## Launch and ownership (last verified 2026-09-06)

Use the managed `pi` zsh function. Brew installs the native CLI on macOS; Linux
uses the existing declarative package group. The function disables native tools
and ambient extensions, then loads the managed workflow and Herdr when present.
Calling `command pi` directly bypasses this managed launch configuration.

The repository's npm manifest/lockfile supplies the extension dependencies and
worker SDK; it does not globally install a second CLI. The pinned SDK is
0.84.4. Re-run the compatibility tests after Brew Pi or extension upgrades.
The existing npm dependency hook installs with lifecycle scripts disabled.

Settings are merged by managed key; unrelated UI/trust preferences survive.
Authentication and session files remain unmanaged. Sign in through Pi's normal
OpenAI subscription login; do not import another harness's auth files.

